From b083d2b3cdea289c3721aaaaf5b451f5b2fcb951 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jraphaelsst <joaoraphaelsst@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 11 May 2026 21:01:47 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] test(pf): add org_id to seeded rows in 23 latent-fail tests
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Surfaced by MOCK-SELECT-PREDICATE-FIX: 23 PF tests seeded rows without org_id while production filters via .eq('org_id', self.org_id). Pre-fix the predicates were tracked-but-not-evaluated by the mock; once SELECT obeys predicates, the tenancy mismatch would silently strip rows.

Fix shape across all 23: add 'org_id': ORG_ID to each seeded row. One exception: test_notificacoes_router.py realigns the seeded notification's user_id to 'test-user-123' (MockUser.id default) — the seed's notificacoes router filters by user_id, not org_id.

No production code touched. All 597 PF tests pass with both current and simulated MOCK-SELECT-PREDICATE-FIX mock behavior.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
